Found during the #66 sondierung (provider facts verified live 2026-08-17 by langertha-llm-advisor).

lib/Langertha/Engine/Gemini.pm builds its endpoint inline at three sites:
  205: $self->url . "/v1beta/models/${model}:generateContent?key=" . $self->api_key
  386: $self->url . "/v1beta/models/${model}:streamGenerateContent?key=" . $self->api_key . "&alt=sse"
  489: $self->url . "/v1beta/models?key=" . $self->api_key

api_key is required (_build_api_key croaks) and update_request only sets content-type. So the
API-key-in-query-string auth and the /v1beta/models/{model} path shape are welded into the
method bodies.

Consequence: the Gemini *envelope* (contents / generationConfig / functionDeclarations /
toolConfig / cachedContent) is already reusable, but no second consumer can be reached, because
every alternative endpoint differs exactly in auth + base path:
  - Vertex AI express mode: https://aiplatform.googleapis.com/v1/publishers/google/models/{m}:generateContent?key=...
    (same ?key= auth! delta is only base URL + publishers/google/models/ prefix + /v1 vs /v1beta)
  - Vertex AI standard:     https://{loc}-aiplatform.googleapis.com/v1/projects/{p}/locations/{loc}/publishers/google/models/{m}:generateContent
    with Authorization: Bearer <ADC token>
  - Gemini-native gateways (e.g. LiteLLM proxy) serve /v1beta/models/{m}:generateContent with Bearer auth

Fix shape (do this WHEN a shim engine is actually wanted, not speculatively): one overridable
model-path/endpoint builder plus an auth seam that can move the credential from the query string
to a header; then `Engine::VertexGemini extends Engine::Gemini` is a small subclass.

Explicitly NOT the fix: extracting Role::GeminiCompatible. The delta between consumers is auth +
URL, never the envelope, so ADR 0006 inheritance covers it; see #66 for the reasoning.

Body deltas a Vertex shim would additionally need to handle: fileData.fileUri wants gs:// on
Vertex (Files API URIs are Developer-API-only), grounding is googleSearch vs Vertex AI Search
retrieval, `labels` is Vertex-side.
Seam implemented (worker-gemini), NOT committed - orchestrator commits.

lib/Langertha/Engine/Gemini.pm: four methods, one override point per delta ADR 0016 names:
  gemini_api_version  -> "v1beta"                       (/v1 vs /v1beta)
  gemini_model_url    -> "models/{model}:{method}"      (publishers/google/models/ prefix)
  gemini_auth_query   -> ( key => api_key )             (query-string vs header credential)
  gemini_url          -> {url}/{version}/{path} + query (shared assembly, auth pairs first)
Base URL stays the existing `url` attribute. The three call sites (chat_request,
chat_stream_request, list_models_request) are now one-liners.

URLs byte-identical, verified by diffing generated URIs before/after, incl. the paginated
listing URL. No existing test changed. New offline pin: t/46_gemini_endpoint_seam.t (15
tests) - the three URLs literally, plus a Test::Gemini::HeaderAuth subclass proving base
URL + version + model path + Bearer-header auth all move by overriding the seam, and that
api_key stays required for the Developer API.

